my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
hello
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{Ctrl-w deletes word backward in insert mode},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/ctrl_w_insert`

Tests that **Ctrl-w** in insert mode deletes the word before the cursor
(including trailing whitespace), similar to how backspace works on words.

**Keys:** `A`, type ` beautiful world`, `Control-w`, `Escape`

**initial.png**
- Buffer contains "hello"
- Cursor at column 0

**after_typing.png**
- Line reads "hello beautiful world" after typing
- Intermediate snapshot showing text before deletion

**after_ctrl_w.png**
- Line reads "hello beautiful" (word "world" deleted by Ctrl-w)
- Cursor at end of "beautiful "
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->key('A');
        $ctx->type(' beautiful world');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_typing');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->key('Control-w');
        $ctx->key('Escape');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_ctrl_w');
    },
}
